            (renamed to Basic, Abel, Kernel, Sinc, Approx, Equation).

    This project retains the declarations needed by its proofs and documented
    renewal interfaces. The vendored subset has the following modifications:
      (1) imports use this project's module paths where needed;
      (2) the renewal-limit chain uses 'FellerNonlattice' in place of the stronger
          upstream 'Nonlattice'. Basic.lean defines that condition and its almost
          everywhere consequence; forwarding declarations and three proof sites
          are adjusted. The original 'Nonlattice' definition and its two
          characteristic-function bounds remain for the proved comparison and
          counterexamples;
      (3) unused helpers are omitted from Basic.lean, Equation.lean and Kernel.lean,
          including the discounted renewal-measure API and the upstream scalar
          limit and angular-reconstruction wrappers. Related documentation is
          updated, including two corrections to comments on non-lattice laws;
      (4) sources use Lean's module system, with public imports and exposed public
          definitions to preserve the retained library interfaces.
    Each file carries a provenance header. See docs/renewal-library.md for the
    retained mathematical interfaces and the non-lattice distinction.

